dialect protocol
protocol semio.value.diff
version 1
schema stdio.semio.value.diff
start body

# REAL binary diff frame, replacing the `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut this
# facet started with (`🦀️component.rs`'s old `DiffCodec::encode_diff`). `SemioValueDiff` is a
# genuine data-carrying recursive enum — no `DslField` impl exists or can exist for it (blanket
# impls cover only ints/bool/String/Vec<T where T: DslField>/BTreeMap/[T;N]/DslValue/Wire, never a
# data-carrying enum) — so the generic derive-based binary layout genuinely does not fit (confirmed
# by re-reading the type, not assumed). Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT`
# convention) + `presence u8` (bit0=`root` present, bit1=`nodes` present) as two REAL fixed
# fields, then 0-2 recursive payloads back-to-back as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain. The
# recursive payload itself is real LEB128-varint-framed binary (`enc_value_diff_bin`/
# `enc_nodes_diff_bin` in the same `🦀️component.rs`, reusing `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/
# `store::ByteReader`) — NOT re-modeled field-by-field here because `Prim::Ref` (the only construct
# that could describe `SemioValue`'s self-recursion at the protocol-dialect level) unconditionally
# errors during `walk_protocol` (recipe §5's `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` gap, re-confirmed by
# every prior pilot). This is the same honest-boundary treatment the plan itself prescribes for a
# compressed payload segment — opaque at the protocol layer, genuinely structured (and round-trip
# tested) at the Rust layer. Same shape json's own `🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`
# uses for its own `has_value u8` twin field.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field presence u8
chain payload bytes
